WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:03.390
- My favorite part about doing murals is

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.768
the opportunity to reach someone that

00:00:06.768 --> 00:00:09.648
usually wouldn't be around me.

00:00:09.648 --> 00:00:12.405
This mural is called "Breathe Deep."

00:00:12.405 --> 00:00:15.095
I believe that you learn your best lessons

00:00:15.095 --> 00:00:16.546
when you're not expecting to learn.

00:00:16.546 --> 00:00:19.796
(upbeat hip hop music)

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:25.640
My name is Fabian Williams.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.004
I'm an artist working in
the great city of Atlanta.

00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:33.504
I've done over a dozen murals in the city.

00:00:35.096 --> 00:00:37.632
I came from advertising, and

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:39.750
the type of work that I used to do

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.917
was primarily to sell
products that you don't need.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.471
At a certain point, I just kinda felt like

00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:51.138
I was using my powers
for the wrong reasons.

00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:59.449
My work is a mix of
race, politics, and ...

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:00.282
humor.

00:01:00.282 --> 00:01:02.131
So I painted Martin Luther King

00:01:02.131 --> 00:01:03.980
floating up in space,
pointing down at you,

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.393
because you have to do the work.

00:01:06.393 --> 00:01:08.119
You have to realize the dream.

00:01:08.119 --> 00:01:12.063
I've come to believe that space is wisdom.

00:01:12.063 --> 00:01:15.547
And when I imagine where
someone like Martin Luther King

00:01:15.547 --> 00:01:19.107
came from and went back
to, it would be space.

00:01:19.107 --> 00:01:23.887
I chose Hosea because his
story is kind of amazing.

00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:26.283
He was a Purple Heat recipient.

00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:29.332
He was like the general of
the Poor People's Campaign

00:01:29.332 --> 00:01:31.001
under Martin Luther King.

00:01:31.001 --> 00:01:32.791
He joined the Civil Rights Movement.

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.754
He did a lot of community building.

00:01:34.754 --> 00:01:37.754
He did a lot of really great things.

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:44.233
The conversation that
I'm having with my work

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.990
is that we need new leaders.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.836
I want someone to walk
by one of those murals

00:01:48.836 --> 00:01:50.647
and feel a connection.

00:01:50.647 --> 00:01:52.968
There's another Hosea Williams here.

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:55.464
There's another Martin
Luther King Jr. here.

00:01:55.464 --> 00:01:58.393
They're walking around here,
they just don't know it yet.

00:01:58.393 --> 00:02:00.073
These kids should be able to get up

00:02:00.073 --> 00:02:03.740
and walk outside the
house and be inspired.

